{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1904 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fda3f8812e774deda953892d8e1926f452bf3bcdb8ac426c8618b9ff9b1f2005" :edb/db-before-t 1903 :edb/db-after-t 1904 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535216 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:46:54.868Z" 13194139535216 true] [17592186147444 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338021 13194139535216 true] [17592186147445 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338031 13194139535216 true] [17592186147445 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338045 13194139535216 true] [17592186147446 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338028 13194139535216 true] [17592186147446 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338059 13194139535216 true] [17592186338021 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338022 13194139535216 true] [17592186338021 1089 "q-331457" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338021 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535216 true] [17592186338021 1100 "Find the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{3t}-{e}^{-t}$ for $s>3.$" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338021 1113 #uuid "fde1c354-d593-5da3-9167-ee1bf6674333" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338021 1145 "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}-{e}^{-t}} & =L{{e}^{3t}}+L{-{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =L{{e}^{3t}}-L{{e}^{-t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,s>3 \\\\ L{{e}^{-t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+1},\\,s>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =L{{e}^{3t}}-L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(s+1)-(s-3)}{(s-3)(s+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{s+1-s+3}{(s-3)(s+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(s-3)(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (3,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-1,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{f(t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(3,\\infty )\\cap (-1,\\infty )=(3,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>3.$" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338023 13194139535216 true] [17592186338022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338024 13194139535216 true] [17592186338022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338025 13194139535216 true] [17592186338022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338026 13194139535216 true] [17592186338022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338027 13194139535216 true] [17592186338022 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535216 true] [17592186338022 1041 "selection" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338022 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338027 13194139535216 true] [17592186338022 1110 #uuid "eada0007-4de9-5471-be45-58c5eb4925dd" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338023 1034 "\\frac{2s}{(s-3)(s+1)}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535216 true] [17592186338023 1111 #uuid "57da5928-7d60-5fba-813c-dc9b71993f6b" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338024 1034 "\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535216 true] [17592186338024 1111 #uuid "a7168acc-33ea-5634-8b11-6ea013081509" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338025 1034 "-\\frac{4}{(s-3)(s+1)}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535216 true] [17592186338025 1111 #uuid "2484cd56-f6c2-5b82-bc38-47b11f42636d" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338026 1034 "\\frac{s+1}{(s-3)(s+1)}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535216 true] [17592186338026 1111 #uuid "b6b3d8cd-b6a5-5fdf-9e47-b6797cb172c6" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338027 1034 "\\frac{4}{(s-3)(s+1)}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535216 true] [17592186338027 1111 #uuid "debb1db8-243d-5dd4-9609-bfbfb4ecdb72" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338028 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338029 13194139535216 true] [17592186338028 1089 "q-331505" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338028 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535216 true] [17592186338028 1100 "Given that for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind the Laplace transform of $f(t)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t$ for $s>0.$\n\n$L{f(t)}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338028 1113 #uuid "0bf4c6b3-b0c5-5df4-8aa1-f94e26ca379d" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338028 1145 "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t} & =L{-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t}+L{6\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t} \\\\  & =-3L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t}+6L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t} & =\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}, &  & s>0, \\\\ L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}, &  & s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+25},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t} & =\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+25},\\,s>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =-3L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t}+6L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+25}+6\\cdot \\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+25} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3s}{{s}^{2}+25}+\\frac{30}{{s}^{2}+25} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3s+30}{{s}^{2}+25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338029 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338030 13194139535216 true] [17592186338029 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535216 true] [17592186338029 1041 "field-1" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338029 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338030 13194139535216 true] [17592186338029 1110 #uuid "0fabe243-f221-5137-8d30-a1130f916221" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338030 1034 "\\frac{30-3s}{s^2+25}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338030 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535216 true] [17592186338030 1111 #uuid "e61cdf0a-5af5-5ec3-84ca-7f628dd0375b" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338031 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338032 13194139535216 true] [17592186338031 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338038 13194139535216 true] [17592186338031 1089 "q-340655" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338031 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535216 true] [17592186338031 1100 "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." 13194139535216 true] [17592186338031 1113 #uuid "42bf59e6-fc11-5187-a3f2-889c117ed67e" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338031 1145 "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)=\\frac{{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{3t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-3t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,s>3 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{3t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-3t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+3)+(s-3)}{(s-3)(s+3)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (3,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-3,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(3,\\infty )\\cap (-3,\\infty )=(3,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>3.$" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338033 13194139535216 true] [17592186338032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338034 13194139535216 true] [17592186338032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338035 13194139535216 true] [17592186338032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338036 13194139535216 true] [17592186338032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338037 13194139535216 true] [17592186338032 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535216 true] [17592186338032 1041 "field-1" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338032 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338037 13194139535216 true] [17592186338032 1110 #uuid "2f915ee1-3ad6-5e9b-8905-49ba2e7d2000" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338033 1034 "\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}-9}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535216 true] [17592186338033 1111 #uuid "968f1c52-6daa-5ebb-8da5-c398a5bb68f5" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338034 1034 "\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535216 true] [17592186338034 1111 #uuid "a8a0b663-3082-539e-b4ea-e8ce7256f18e" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338035 1034 "\\frac{3s}{{s}^{2}-9}" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535216 true] [17592186338035 1111 #uuid "18d4cdb5-1632-5d54-8694-6f3e6b506e15" 13194139535216 true] [17592186338036 1034 "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}" 1319413